+## unsmell run 2026-11-02 (`EventSignatureRow` struct)
+
+- **Two types for one cached event record.** `EventSignatureRow`
+  (`src/evm/cache/event_signature_cache.rs`) and `signatures::ResolvedEvent`
+  have the same three fields. The adapter in `src/bin/chainfold/signature_cache.rs`
+  copies one into the other in `get` and takes it apart again in `put`. Options:
+  (a) delete `EventSignatureRow`. Then `get_event_signature` returns
+  `Option<ResolvedEvent>`, `insert_event_signature` takes `&ResolvedEvent`, and
+  the adapter only maps errors. (b) Keep both types and add
+  `From<EventSignatureRow> for ResolvedEvent` in `evm::cache`. Recommended: (a).
+  Either way, `insert_event_signature` should take the record as one value
+  instead of `signature, topic0, abi_json`. The tests can then compare whole
+  rows with the `PartialEq` derive. Patch: `.git/unsmell/20261102-005400/fixes/t3.patch`.
+- **Cache key travels as three values.** `(chain_id, address, event_name)` goes
+  through `get_event_signature`, `insert_event_signature`, `SignatureCache::get`
+  and `put`, `resolve_event` and `resolve_event_topic`. Make it one key type. The
+  `signatures` copy must stay chainfold-free (raw `u64`/`[u8; 20]`). Patch:
+  `fixes/t5.patch`.
+- **Dead constructors.** `EventSignatureCache::open` has no callers, and
+  `open_in_memory` is only used by the file's own tests. Delete both, and have
+  the tests use `CacheDb::open_in_memory()?.signatures()`. Patch: `fixes/t4.patch`.
+- **U256 BLOB decode written twice.** `src/evm/cache/erc20_cache.rs` reads a
+  `Vec<u8>`, checks `len() == 32` and maps a wrong length to `None` in two
+  queries. Give it one named decode in `src/evm/cache.rs`. Patch: `fixes/t6.patch`.
